+
+## Recovery handoff after a failed edit
+
+A failed patch or diff is diagnosed by a later successful exact `read_file` of
+that same target. When the live recovery governor reaches `Fix`, that completed
+diagnosis belongs to the still-pending edit and survives native session JSON
+roundtrip, runtime `Continue`, and Coder-Observer handoff. The restored governor
+may therefore return to `Fix` for the same edit instead of blocking it again as
+`Diagnose`.
+
+This survival is deliberately narrow. It applies only while the completed
+diagnosis still belongs to the current failure. A newer failed check, including
+a different command, a failed edit to another target, or a failed read starts a
+new failure boundary and keeps its own diagnosis obligation. Absent, stale,
+unrelated, or uncorrelated reads and assistant assertions are not evidence.
+
+Reading is diagnosis, never repair or verification. The failed-edit count and
+the pending original exact check remain intact until an actual repair and a
+fresh successful verification satisfy the existing gates.
diff --git a/src/tui/agent/edit_failure.rs b/src/tui/agent/edit_failure.rs
